  "Item0000000020": {
   "description": "Forward elimination transforms A to an upper-triangular U using row operations and (usually) partial pivoting; back-substitution then solves Ux=b. This is the workhorse of dense linear algebra and forms the basis for LU factorization used by LAPACK and most libraries.",
   "id": "Q6825760",
   "label": "Classical Gaussian elimination with pivoting plus back-substitution for dense linear systems",
   "payload": {
