  "Item0000000021": {
   "description": "Row-reduction with both forward elimination and full back-elimination to produce RREF and, optionally, A^{-1} by augmenting with the identity. Robust pivoting strategies are essential; numerical stability is generally inferior to LU with partial pivoting for solving Ax=b. This method is pedagogically transparent but rarely used in production solvers for dense systems.",
   "id": "Q6825773",
   "label": "Gauss-Jordan elimination to compute reduced row-echelon form and matrix inverses",
   "payload": {
